# 7. SINGLE ADMIN AND MULTI-USER ACCOUNT SYSTEM

This is a critical business requirement.

Every company starts with a minimum of ONE user.

The first registered account becomes the company's primary administrator.

## Single-user company

When a company has purchased or received a one-user plan:

- Only one user account is allowed.
- The primary administrator uses their own username/email and password.
- No additional user creation is available.
- No role selector appears at login.
- The company operates with one administrator account.
- The administrator can access the ERP modules permitted by the plan.

Do not force a single-user company to create multiple users.

## Multi-user company

When a company purchases a package allowing multiple users, enable the user management module.

